Oxikube GPUI overlay patch: draw a late resize at once, in the resize's own transaction
Crate: gpui-pre-macos 0.3.7 (crates.io, Apache-2.0; snapshot of zed-industries/zed@1a28cff,
Copyright Zed Industries, Inc. and contributors). Zed path: crates/gpui_macos/src/{window.rs,display_link.rs}
Upstream: Zed PR draft "gpui_macos: Draw a resized window at once when its display pass is late"
(not yet filed; Oxikube issue karan-vk/Oxikube#601). Drop this patch at the first gpui-pre bump
that contains the fix.
Patch: Copyright Oxikube contributors, GPL-3.0-or-later (see patches/gpui/README.md).

Why: during a live resize every frame is drawn by the layer's display pass (`display_layer`,
presented with the Core Animation transaction), which AppKit runs once per refresh after the
window's frame changed. When the main thread comes back late from the previous frame's commit
(the window server answers late), the new size arrives after that refresh's pass and its frame
waits a whole further pass: the window misses a refresh (E05-P601: 53 to 129 per 10 s sweep).
`set_frame_size` now draws the frame itself, presented in the same transaction as the new
size, when a refresh or more has passed since the window last asked for a frame. Otherwise the
display pass draws it as before, so a window never draws faster than its display refreshes.
`WindowFrameSource::refresh_interval` reads the display link's period for that test.
